            <ArticleTitle>Implications for port placement of deep circumflex iliac artery damage at laparoscopy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>221-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A cannula injury to the deep circumflex iliac vessels led to substantial morbidity and required surgical repair. Surgeons must increase their awareness of the anatomy of these vessels and place laparoscopic ports to minimize the risk of injury. (J Am Assoc Gynecol Laparosc 6(2):221-223, 1999)</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
